# Developer tooling and reference material; the deployment does not use these.
# The schema is applied to Supabase as a migration, never by the running app.
#
# The leading slash on /scripts is load-bearing. Unanchored, these patterns match
# a directory of that name at ANY depth — so `scripts` also excluded
# client/scripts, which holds the step that stages the OCR engine's runtime files
# before the client is built. The file was committed and pushed, and then simply
# was not there: "Cannot find module client/scripts/copy-ocr-assets.mjs", and the
# production build failed. Anchor anything meant to name a directory at the root.
docs
/scripts
supabase
